/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/HMerEtOH-formation.dat -- the 2-mercaptoethanol master as the sum of its fully dissociated form (the inverse of the records written from the master; a case declares one master and the closure activates the record reachable from it):
      MerEtOH(-1) + 1 H+  <=>  HMerEtOH
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 9.75, dH1 = 26.2 kJ/mol (grade CB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  This record carries the one step (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  Goldberg gives no formation data for a buffer.  The species are the acid form(s) and the conjugate base(s) of the section, charges as the section states them, the formula the section's own empirical formula.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species HMerEtOH; masters ( { ion MerEtOH; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 1; } );
      logK25 9.75; dH -26200; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.43, p. 308: pK1 9.75, dH1 26.2 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
